<section class="page-header">
<div class="container">
<p style="margin-bottom:8px;"><a href="/blog/" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);font-size:0.9rem;text-decoration:none;">&larr; Back to Blog</a></p>
<h1>Does Your Car Insurance Cover a Rental? What to Check Before Pickup</h1>
<p>Five questions for your agent, and the one vehicle type where the answer is most likely to change.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section">
<div class="container">
<div style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;">
<p>One of the three things we ask for at pickup is proof of your own auto insurance &mdash; the policy number and the expiration date. Most renters have it on their phone. What fewer renters have is a clear answer to the real question: <em>what does my policy actually cover while I'm driving a rental?</em></p>
<p>We're a rental company, not an insurance agency, so we won't tell you what your policy says. But after four decades of handing over keys, we know which questions matter. Here they are.</p>
<h2>Five questions to ask your agent</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Does my coverage extend to a rental vehicle?</strong> Many personal auto policies carry over to a rental car used for personal driving. Confirm it.</li>
<li><strong>Do my collision and comprehensive apply, or just liability?</strong> If you only carry liability on your own car, damage to the rental may not be covered.</li>
<li><strong>What's my deductible?</strong> That's likely what you'd owe out of pocket if something happens.</li>
<li><strong>Does it cover the vehicle type I'm renting?</strong> This is the big one for groups &mdash; see below.</li>
<li><strong>Does it cover loss of use?</strong> Some policies cover the time a damaged rental is out of service; some don't.</li>
</ol>
<h2>The van question</h2>
<p>Cars, SUVs, and minivans are usually straightforward. Large passenger vans are where policies differ most &mdash; some personal policies and many credit card rental benefits exclude vehicles over a certain seating capacity. If you're renting our <a href="15-passenger-van-rental-cost-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">15-passenger van</a> for a team, church, or reunion, ask your agent about it by name. Churches and organizations often have a separate commercial or non-owned auto policy that's the right fit.</p>
<h2>Don't count on the credit card alone</h2>
<p>Card rental benefits can be useful, but they're often secondary to your personal policy and frequently exclude large vans and longer rental periods. Read the fine print or call the number on the back of the card.</p>
<h2>If you're renting because your car's in the shop</h2>
<p>That's a different path. With <a href="insurance-replacement-rental-cars-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">insurance replacement rentals</a>, the at-fault carrier or your own rental reimbursement coverage often pays, and we work directly with adjusters and body shops across western Wisconsin. Get your claim number and call us &mdash; we'll handle a lot of the back-and-forth. Need it today? See <a href="same-day-insurance-replacement-rental-black-river-falls" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">same-day replacement</a>.</p>
<h2>What to bring</h2>
<p>License, card, and your insurance card or app showing the policy number and expiration date. That's it &mdash; the full list is in our <a href="what-you-need-to-rent-a-car-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">first-timer&rsquo;s guide</a>. Questions about a specific trip? <strong>Call or text 715-396-1466.</strong></p>
<div style="margin-top:48px;">
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-list">
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">What proof of insurance do I need to rent a car at Riverside Auto Rental?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Proof of your own auto insurance showing the policy number and expiration date. An insurance card or your insurer's app works.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Does my personal car insurance cover a rental car?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Many personal policies extend to a rental used for personal driving, but coverage varies. Ask your agent whether collision and comprehensive apply and what your deductible is.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Is a 15-passenger van covered by personal auto insurance?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>It depends on the policy. Some personal policies and many credit card benefits exclude large passenger vans, so ask your agent about the 15-passenger van specifically before you rent.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Who pays for a rental while my car is being repaired after an accident?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Often the at-fault driver's insurer or your own rental reimbursement coverage. We work directly with adjusters and body shops; bring your claim number.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
